content:
Cash purchases show need beyond the limit. On the authorization owed after an overturned quantity limit denial on an acute migraine drug under the Utilization Management Program, paper claims for the drug under the Retail Pharmacy Network Benefit denied because a coverage review was required add units to the overturn ceiling:

- 2 or more such denials dated within the last 3 months: 2 units;
- exactly 1 such denial: 1 unit;
- none: nothing.

The 3 months end on the date the authorization is put in force: a denial counts when it is dated after the same day of the month three months before that date. Only denials of paper claims for the same drug, for the reason that a coverage review was required, count.

*Hypothetical case:* authorization put in force on 15 October; qualifying denials on 1 August and 15 July. Three months before is 15 July, so only the 1 August denial counts: 1 unit.
